{"deps":{"riantr/moonbit_image":"0.3.9","moonbit-community/proton":"0.9.0","moonbit-community/proton_contract":"0.9.0"},"name":"riantr/moonbit_labeler","readme":"README.mbt.md","yanked":false,"license":"MIT","version":"0.2.16","checksum":"1b8c389d4690c4c7cd6cd6b290762a4fa1c9da54349a1555e49c5f0825800f6f","keywords":["labeling","image-annotation","voc","yolo","moonbit","ipc","json-rpc"],"warn_list":"","created_at":"2026-11-12T19:48:40.069679+00:00","repository":"https://github.com/riantr/moonbit-labeler","description":"Image / video labeling backend for the MoonBit Labeler app: 27 async ops over @fs/@json for folder browsing, image IO, label IO, schema normalization (parse/serialize round-trip), class management (including the class rename), per-frame video labels, and VOC/YOLO/COCO export. The op_handlers are pure async MoonBit functions and can be wired into any IPC layer (Proton/CEF, stdio JSON-RPC, HTTP, WASM, custom bridge). Includes a `pub async fn dispatch_op(op : String, payload : Json) -> Json` entry point (in `extensions/labeler`) for embedding outside the CEF runtime; the package is native-only, so a consuming package must declare `supported_targets = \\\"native\\\"`.","yanked_reason":null,"preferred_target":"native","supported_targets":"+native"}
